## Solution

We compute
$$\mathbf{E}(|X|^{1-\varepsilon})=\frac{1}{\pi}\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}\frac{|x|^{1-\varepsilon}}{1+x^2}\,dx=\frac{2}{\pi}\int_{0}^{\infty}\frac{x^{1-\varepsilon}}{1+x^2}\,dx.$$

**Substitution.** Set $x=\tan\theta$, $dx=\sec^{2}\theta\,d\theta$, $1+x^{2}=\sec^{2}\theta$. Then
$$\frac{x^{1-\varepsilon}}{1+x^{2}}\,dx=\tan^{1-\varepsilon}\theta\,d\theta,\qquad \theta:0\to\tfrac{\pi}{2}.$$
Hence
$$I(\varepsilon):=\int_{0}^{\infty}\frac{x^{1-\varepsilon}}{1+x^{2}}\,dx=\int_{0}^{\pi/2}\tan^{1-\varepsilon}\theta\,d\theta.$$

**Beta-function evaluation.** Writing $\tan^{a}\theta=\sin^{a}\theta\,\cos^{-a}\theta$ with $a=1-\varepsilon$,
$$\int_{0}^{\pi/2}\sin^{a}\theta\,\cos^{-a}\theta\,d\theta=\frac{1}{2}B\!\left(\frac{a+1}{2},\frac{1-a}{2}\right)=\frac{1}{2}\,\frac{\Gamma\!\left(\frac{a+1}{2}\right)\Gamma\!\left(\frac{1-a}{2}\right)}{\Gamma(1)}.$$
Using the reflection formula $\Gamma(z)\Gamma(1-z)=\dfrac{\pi}{\sin(\pi z)}$ with $z=\dfrac{a+1}{2}$,
$$\Gamma\!\left(\frac{a+1}{2}\right)\Gamma\!\left(\frac{1-a}{2}\right)=\frac{\pi}{\sin\!\left(\frac{\pi(a+1)}{2}\right)}=\frac{\pi}{\cos\!\left(\frac{\pi a}{2}\right)}.$$
Therefore
$$I(\varepsilon)=\frac{\pi}{2\cos\!\left(\frac{\pi(1-\varepsilon)}{2}\right)}=\frac{\pi}{2\sin\!\left(\frac{\pi\varepsilon}{2}\right)},$$
valid for $\varepsilon\in(0,2)$ (so that $a=1-\varepsilon\in(-1,1)$).

**Assembling.**
$$\mathbf{E}(|X|^{1-\varepsilon})=\frac{2}{\pi}\,I(\varepsilon)=\frac{2}{\pi}\cdot\frac{\pi}{2\sin\!\left(\frac{\pi\varepsilon}{2}\right)}=\frac{1}{\sin\!\left(\frac{\pi\varepsilon}{2}\right)}.$$

**The limit.**
$$\varepsilon\,\mathbf{E}(|X|^{1-\varepsilon})=\frac{\varepsilon}{\sin\!\left(\frac{\pi\varepsilon}{2}\right)}.$$
Since $\sin\!\left(\frac{\pi\varepsilon}{2}\right)\sim\frac{\pi\varepsilon}{2}$ as $\varepsilon\searrow 0$,
$$\lim_{\varepsilon\searrow 0}\varepsilon\,\mathbf{E}(|X|^{1-\varepsilon})=\lim_{\varepsilon\searrow 0}\frac{\varepsilon}{\frac{\pi\varepsilon}{2}}=\boxed{\frac{2}{\pi}}.$$

